<!--
    No AppCompat/Material Components library is a dependency (Compose draws every pixel), so this
    extends a built-in platform theme, not Theme.AppCompat.*/Theme.MaterialComponents.* — "DayNight"
    itself is an AppCompat concept, not a platform one (confirmed: android:Theme.Material.DayNight
    doesn't link at all). DeviceDefault already tracked this device's system dark setting before this
    theme existed (the very first screenshot of the unthemed app was already dark), so it needs no
    equivalent here — only NoActionBar: without it, the platform's default decor ActionBar showed
    the app label ("Kalita") above Compose's own header row, which already shows the same title — a
    visibly duplicated, wasted top row.
-->
<resources>
    <style name="Theme.Kalita" parent="android:Theme.DeviceDefault.NoActionBar" />

    <!--
        The boot splash (dev_plan.md Этап 10, FR-A8 "адаптивная компоновка и тема" — the same
        срез's spirit, finishing the launch-time first impression): without any android:icon at
        all (found live — the system showed a generic placeholder, not a Kalita identity, at every
        launch), the platform's own default splash had nothing to show either. Theme.SplashScreen
        (androidx.core:core-splashscreen) needs no AppCompat/Material Components, same as
        Theme.Kalita's own base — set directly on the Activity (not Application) per the library's
        own documented pattern, with postSplashScreenTheme swapping back to Theme.Kalita once
        MainActivity.installSplashScreen() hands off.
    -->
    <style name="Theme.Kalita.Starting" parent="Theme.SplashScreen">
        <item name="windowSplashScreenBackground">#1B1F2A</item>
        <item name="windowSplashScreenAnimatedIcon">@drawable/splash_rings_animated</item>
        <item name="windowSplashScreenAnimationDuration">1000</item>
        <item name="postSplashScreenTheme">@style/Theme.Kalita</item>
    </style>
</resources>
